  L3 h2 "Why We're Building This"
  L58 h2 "The Beta Build (Launch Target TBD pending scoping)"
  L60 h3 "Individual Trader Beta - Q2 Target (Marketed as “The Helm”)"
  L113 h3 "6-Month Vision (End of Q3 MVP)"
  L138 h2 "Application Suite 2-Year Vision (2026 – 2028)"
  L140 h3 "One Product That Grows With You"
  L277 h3 "What This Requires From the Platform"
  L295 h2 "How This Connects to Science & Algorithms + Trading Teams"
  L313 h2 "Open Questions"
=== LINES ===
[000] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H1
      "😎 "
      "Core Applications 2026 Vision" {b fg=#337ea9}
[001] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#337ea9}
[002] indent=0 block=-
[003] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H2
      "Why We're Building This" {b fg=#337ea9}
[004] indent=0 block=-
[005] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Through our design sprints, customer research, and direct work with "
[006] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "enterprise customers, we heard the same pain point over and over: "
[007] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "workflow fragmentation. Traders spend hours every morning toggling "
[008] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "between weather sites, market data platforms, spreadsheets, and internal"
[009] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "tools just to build a picture of what kind of day it is. The analysis "
[010] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "that should take 10 minutes takes two hours, and most of that time is "
[011] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "gathering context, not making decisions. "
[012] indent=0 block=-
[013] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "Two things are driving this effort: we have emerging product-market fit "
[014] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "with our enterprise customers, and the competitive landscape has shifted"
[015] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "with agentic AI. We're doubling down on what's working, with some "
[016] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "targeted tweaks."
[017] indent=0 block=-
[018] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Our enterprise engagements (NRG, BP, Gunvor) have validated that EQ's "
[019] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "platform solves real problems for real traders. But enterprise sales "
[020] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "cycles are long, resource-intensive, and vulnerable to single points of "
[021] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "failure if there are skeptical users. We are targeting the hardest, most"
[022] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "expensive place to enter a customer relationship: the top of the "
[023] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "enterprise. A common application suite with progressive access levels "
[024] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "changes this for our customers and for us.  An individual trader signs "
[025] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "up and immediately gets value of workflow fragmentation relief through "
[026] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "unified market data, probabilistic forecasts, AI-native capabilities, "
[027] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "and full transparency into the data behind every assumption (what we "
[028] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "call \"glass box\"). No enterprise sales cycle required. We build brand "
[029] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "rapport with individual users, then provide the right hooks and carrots "
[030] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "to encourage them deeper into our enterprise solutions. This is the "
[031] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "tweaked GTM motion: lower friction entry, brand recognition with "
[032] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "individual users, and natural expansion into team and enterprise "
[033] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "contracts."
[034] indent=0 block=-
[035] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "As customers invest more, the platform grows with them. Bring your own "
[036] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "data, forecasts, and strategies into the same unified surface, and our "
[037] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "AI workflows seamlessly pick them up. Connect your existing pipelines "
[038] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "through our APIs and SDKs. Our enterprise platform offering is the "
[039] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "infrastructure that enables traders to understand markets, evaluate "
[040] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "positions, and take action, whether EQ develops strategies for them or "
[041] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "they develop their own."
[042] indent=0 block=-
[043] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "What makes this approach sticky is not any single feature. It's that "
[044] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "each layer of investment compounds. Workflow embedding gets us in "
[045] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "(traders adopt because it replaces the 20-tab morning routine, not "
[046] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "because we sold them a feature list). Speaking trader language from day "
[047] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "one means zero learning curve due to exceptional UX. Co-optimization "
[048] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "across market products (DART + CRRs + futures + gas on one platform) "
[049] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "creates value no individual tool can replicate. And intelligence that "
[050] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "learns, remembers, and compounds over time means a trader who's used the"
[051] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "product for six months has a system that understands how they think. "
[052] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Switching means starting over."
[053] indent=0 block=-
[054] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[055] indent=0 block=-
[056] indent=0 block=335dbe27
[057] indent=0 block=-
[058] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H2
      "The Beta Build (Launch Target TBD pending scoping)" {b fg=#337ea9}
[059] indent=0 block=-
[060] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H3
      "Individual Trader Beta - Q2 Target (Marketed as “The Helm”)" {b}
[061] indent=0 block=-
[062] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "What it is:" {b}
      " Invite-only beta, ~12-20 users, full-featured trial. Design "
[063] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "partner program that validates the PLG motion and generates real usage "
[064] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "data."
[065] indent=0 block=-
[066] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Features Scope:" {b}
[067] indent=0 block=-
[068] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Explorer:" {b}
      " Probabilistic price forecasts, market data, constraint "
[069] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "analysis, system-wide views. Unified data layer replacing the 20-tab "
[070] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "workflow."
[071] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "AI Chat:" {b}
      " Agentic analysis grounded in EQ's 60+ code frameworks. Not "
[072] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "generic summaries; power-industry-native intelligence with full "
[073] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "transparency on reasoning."
[074] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Constraints deep dive:" {b}
      " Automated backstory and context for individual "
[075] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "constraints (the \"hour of research in 10 minutes\" use case)."
[076] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Lineage (fast follow):" {b}
      " DAG visibility showing data sources, "
[077] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "transformations, and point-in-time correctness. Every number has a "
[078] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "receipt."
[079] indent=0 block=-
[080] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD Scope:" {b}
[081] indent=0 block=-
[082] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to understand what kind of day tomorrow is as "
[083] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "quickly as possible"
[084] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to be able to do constraint analysis before bid "
[085] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "close to find potential high-return opportunities"
[086] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to ask a question and get an answer grounded in "
[087] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "power market fundamentals, not generic AI"
[088] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I don’t trust others to understand the complexities of my "
[089] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "work, so I want to be able to interrogate all of the assumptions that "
[090] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "i’m provided (forecasts, chat responses, market summaries, etc)"
[091] indent=0 block=-
[092] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "What is NOT in beta:" {b}
[093] indent=0 block=-
[094] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No portfolio data"
[095] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No SCED what-if scenarios"
[096] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No strategy/forecast workbench"
[097] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No BYO Forecast integration"
[098] indent=0 block=-
[099] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Science dependencies for beta:" {b}
      " Minimal. Beta uses existing probabilistic"
[100] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "forecasts and market data already in the platform. No new model "
[101] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "development required."
[102] indent=0 block=-
[103] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Architecture:" {b}
      " Beta proceeds without ArchV2. Learnings from beta feed "
[104] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "ArchV2 requirements. Beta stack to be defined by engineering & "
[105] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "infrastructure."
[106] indent=0 block=-
[107] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Release cadence:" {b}
      " New feature every 1-2 weeks. Feedback loop through "
[108] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "release notes + direct user feedback requests."
[109] indent=0 block=-
[110] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Beta users:" {b}
      " Currently users from 2+ companies. Max 20 users total. "
[111] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Controlled rollout, not public."
[112] indent=0 block=-
[113] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H3
      "6-Month Vision (End of Q3 MVP)" {b}
[114] indent=0 block=-
[115] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Q3 MVP (OKR2.2 Target: October)"
[116] indent=0 block=-
[117] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "What it is:" {b}
      " A self-serve, low friction entry point onto our platform and"
[118] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "application suite not limited to design partners"
[119] indent=0 block=-
[120] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "What changes from beta to MVP:" {b}
[121] indent=0 block=-
[122] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Users can self-serve sign-up and pay with credit card"
[123] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Core Applications & SA & Delivery propose feature graduation criteria "
[124] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "by end of beta based on customer usage and feedback"
[125] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "GTM finalize pricing plan"
[126] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "OKR1.5: […] The Helm "
      "MVP" {i}
      " by end of Q3’26. Add 20 paid subscribers by "
[127] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "the end of Q4’26 to drive $60K in new ARR."
[128] indent=0 block=-
[129] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Architecture" {b}
      ": Multi-tenant environment, detailed requirements to be put "
[130] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "together with engineering & infrastructure"
[131] indent=0 block=-
[132] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Release cadence: " {b}
      "Continue our Beta momentum with new features every 1-2 "
[133] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "weeks. Ideally SA & Delivery also can choose to release these features "
[134] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "to enterprise customers."
[135] indent=0 block=-
[136] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[137] indent=0 block=-
[138] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H2
      "Application Suite 2-Year Vision (2026 – 2028)" {b fg=#337ea9}
[139] indent=0 block=-
[140] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H3
      "One Product That Grows With You" {b}
[141] indent=0 block=-
[142] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "This is one application suite. It starts as an individual trader's daily"
[143] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "operating environment and scales as customers invest more: more data, "
[144] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "more users, more automation, more integration. We use \"doors\" to "
[145] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "describe natural expansion moments, not tiers or gates, because a "
[146] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "customer can enter through any door and does not need to proceed "
[147] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "sequentially. Each door is an \"I want more\" signal where the platform "
[148] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "meets the customer where they are. There are value levers that can be "
[149] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "controlled throughout the application to help control the funnel and GTM"
[150] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "motion as well (usage caps, limitations on scenarios, limitations on "
[151] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "agents, etc.)."
[152] indent=0 block=-
[153] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Door 1: Individual Trader" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want an army of analysts at my back\"" {i}
[154] indent=0 block=-
[155] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "An individual trader signs up and gets immediate value: unified market "
[156] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "data, probabilistic forecasts at every node, constraint analysis with "
[157] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "automated AI investigation, cross-commodity views, and full system "
[158] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "visualization with weather, wind, and temperature layers over time. "
[159] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Glass box transparency on every number. But this isn't just a dashboard."
[160] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "From day one, traders have agents that help them explore: research a "
[161] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "constraint move, investigate a price spike, run a scenario to test an "
[162] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "intuition, generate a performance attribution report. AI chat grounded "
[163] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "in EQ's analytical frameworks turns questions into analysis, not just "
[164] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "answers. The platform learns the trader's patterns, preferences, and "
[165] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "past analyses through personal context memory. Custom views, saved "
[166] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "prompts, and personalized layouts make it theirs."
[167] indent=0 block=-
[168] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → grow from “Help me understand” (Beta) to “help me investigate and"
[169] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "act on my thinking”"
[170] indent=0 block=-
[171] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to test a hypothesis about what happens to my "
[172] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "positions if gas spikes or wind drops, without building a spreadsheet"
[173] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to be alerted when something changes that affects my"
[174] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "positions, not discover it during my morning routine"
[175] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want the system to remember my patterns and preferences "
[176] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "so it gets smarter the more I use it"
[177] indent=0 block=-
[178] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Door 2: My Data" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want my data and forecasts in here\"" {i}
[179] indent=0 block=-
[180] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Customers bring their own forecasts, proprietary data, and market views "
[181] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "into the same unified surface. This triggers an isolated environment and"
[182] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "unlocks a vertical AI for power which includes portfolio-aware AI and "
[183] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "memory. The platform now reasons over their world, not just the market. "
[184] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Our AI workflows seamlessly pick up customer data alongside EQ's, "
[185] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "organized, versioned, and queryable. EQ offers white-glove service to "
[186] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "make this an exceptional experience for our customers with integrations "
[187] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "starting at this point and at every integration point in the additional "
[188] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "doors. These engagements are where Product learns what to 'productize'. "
[189] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "The patterns SA & Delivery sees across enterprise customers become the "
[190] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "templates and workflows that scale through the offering."
[191] indent=0 block=-
[192] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → shifts from EQ’s world to the customer’s own alpha"
[193] indent=0 block=-
[194] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want the same AI and analysis capabilities applied to my "
[195] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "proprietary data, not just market data"
[196] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to bring my own forecasts in and see them with the "
[197] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "same glass box treatment"
[198] indent=0 block=-
[199] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Door 3: My Strategies" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want to build and run strategies on this\"" {i}
[200] indent=0 block=-
[201] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "The shift from exploration to operations. Door 1 agents help you "
[202] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "understand the market. Door 3 expands to run your trading business. "
[203] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Strategy pipelines, automated briefings, backtesting across historical "
[204] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "conditions. Agents that follow Science and Strategy's proven analytical "
[205] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "workflows: run a DART analysis, evaluate a CRR position, stress-test a "
[206] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "gas portfolio using the same artifacts and methodologies our quants use "
[207] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "internally. The platform tracks what worked and why through operational "
[208] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "memory. Co-optimization across market products (DART + CRRs + futures + "
[209] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "gas) creates value no individual tool can replicate. The 2-year "
[210] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "trajectory is from EQ-assisted to fully self-serve. Customers have told "
[211] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "us directly that they want to build it themselves. Product's job is to "
[212] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "make that possible by turning what we've learned from enterprise "
[213] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "engagements into capabilities any user can access independently."
[214] indent=0 block=-
[215] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → shifts from analysis to operations"
[216] indent=0 block=-
[217] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to be able to easily research, build, monitor, and"
[218] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "deploy strategies"
[219] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to evaluate how my strategy performs across a "
[220] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "range of market conditions before I commit capital"
[221] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to know what's actually driving my PnL"
[222] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk, we want to see our portfolio together, understand our "
[223] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "strategy interactions and behaviors, and maximize risk adjusted return"
[224] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "across all of our individual work"
[225] indent=0 block=-
[226] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "Door 4: My Team" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want my team to have these capabilities\"" {i}
[227] indent=0 block=-
[228] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "A desk lead notices the value. Shared workspaces, team memory that "
[229] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "cross-pollinates context across the desk, shared prompt libraries and "
[230] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "agent results. The buying authority shifts from personal credit card to "
[231] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "team budget. The transition is concierge-assisted, not a migration."
[232] indent=0 block=-
[233] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "JTBD → grows from individual to collective intelligence"
[234] indent=0 block=-
[235] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk lead, I want my team to share context without scheduling a "
[236] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "meeting"
[237] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a team, we want our best analyst's research to benefit everyone, "
[238] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "not live in one person's head or desktop"
[239] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk lead, I want visibility into what my team is watching and "
[240] indent=0 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "what they might be missing"
[241] indent=0 block=-
[242] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Door 5: My Enterprise" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want to embed PowerOS into my systems\"" {i}
[243] indent=0 block=-
[244] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "The product is no longer standalone. SDK access, API integrations, "
[245] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "ETRM/EMS connectors. Customer engineering teams build on EQ's "
[246] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "primitives. DAG-driven real-time updates as new data arrives. "
[247] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Cross-system reasoning and memory span EQ and connected tools. SSO, "
[248] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "compliance certifications, self-serve extensions."
[249] indent=0 block=-
[250] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a technical user, I want to build on EQ's capabilities with my own "
[251] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "tools and code, not be limited to what the UI offers"
[252] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a firm, I want my team to be able to build, modify, and maintain "
[253] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "our own workflows on this platform without submitting a ticket and "
[254] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "waiting for EQ to do it for us"
[255] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As an engineering team, I want one API surface that works the same way"
[256] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "whether I'm powering a dashboard, an automated pipeline, or an agent"
[257] indent=0 block=-
[258] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Door 6: Self-Service" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want this running my org\"" {i}
[259] indent=0 block=-
[260] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Org-wide deployment, cross-desk intelligence, institutional memory that "
[261] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "compounds over years. Users build their own workflows, agents, and "
[262] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "strategies on the platform. Full self-serve application customization: "
[263] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "users vibe-code their own views and tools. A trader who's been on the "
[264] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Helm for six months has a system that understands how they think. An "
[265] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "organization that's been on it for a year has an institutional memory "
[266] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "that no individual departure can erase. This is where EQ's moat becomes "
[267] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "existential, because switching means starting over."
[268] indent=0 block=-
[269] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a head of trading, I want intelligence that compounds across desks,"
[270] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "not just within them. What the gas desk learns about a regime shift "
[271] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "should inform the power desk automatically."
[272] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a COO, I want institutional knowledge that survives when my best "
[273] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "trader leaves"
[274] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a firm, I want my people building their own tools and workflows on "
[275] indent=0 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "this platform, not waiting for a vendor roadmap"
[276] indent=0 block=-
[277] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H3
      "What This Requires From the Platform" {b}
[278] indent=0 block=-
[279] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "The doors describe what customers experience. Underneath, the platform "
[280] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "needs to evolve to support it. That's where architecture v2 comes in."
[281] indent=0 block=-
[282] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "We want to make sure SA & Delivery can easily deploy core features from "
[283] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "the core application suite to enterprise customers, that we can grow our"
[284] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "capabilities horizontally FAST, and that we can explore > build > ship "
[285] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "new features in fast iteration. We also want to make sure there's "
[286] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "alignment between the APIs & primitives that power internal "
[287] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "applications, customer-facing integrations, and agents so we can provide"
[288] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "a unified customer experience. Agents are present from Door 1 (scenario "
[289] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "agents, research agents) and scale in sophistication through Door 6 "
[290] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "(org-wide agent fleets, custom-trained models). The infrastructure needs"
[291] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "to support the full spectrum."
[292] indent=0 block=-
[293] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[294] indent=0 block=-
[295] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H2
      "How This Connects to Science & Algorithms + Trading Teams" {b fg=#337ea9}
[296] indent=0 block=-
[297] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "Beta (now – June):" {b}
      " Science dependencies are minimal. Existing "
[298] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "probabilistic forecasts and market data. No new model development needed"
[299] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "for beta scope."
[300] indent=0 block=-
[301] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "MVP (Q3):" {b}
      " MVP Science scope to be defined jointly with Tyler based on "
[302] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "beta signal. What-if is not critical path for MVP."
[303] indent=0 block=-
[304] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "2-Year:" {b}
      " Central to the full vision. SCED what-if scenarios, "
[305] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "co-optimization across market products, new market expansion (gas, "
[306] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "futures, ftrs, etc.). EQ's application suite makes our best thinking "
[307] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "accessible at scale. Workflows, skills, and predefined artifacts turn "
[308] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "proven methodologies into capabilities any user can leverage, whether EQ"
[309] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "develops the strategies or the customer develops their own."
[310] indent=0 block=-
[311] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[312] indent=0 block=-
[313] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H2
      "Open Questions" {b fg=#337ea9}
[314] indent=0 block=-
[315] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "1. "
      "How do we communicate the application suite framing externally? "
[316] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "   "
      "(naming is \"early discovery,\" not finalized for GTM)"
[317] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "2. "
      "ArchV2 sequencing: how does Helm beta feed ArchV2 priorities vs. "
[318] indent=0 block=335dbe27
      "   "
      "other demand signals?"
